body:
I recommend replacing:
```
RDG::ResourceTracker **trackers = nullptr;
RDG::ResourceUsage *usages = nullptr;
```

With
```
thread_local LocalVector<RDG::ResourceTracker *> trackers;
thread_local LocalVector<RDG::ResourceUsage> usages;
trackers.resize(resource_count);
usages.resize(resource_count);
```
The re-allocation concern the comment indicates is not true. `LocalVector` won't reallocate if the size shrinks, the capacity will remain as big as possible. It behaves in the same way as std::vector does (this is not true for regular `Vector`).

Unlike `Vector`, the [] operator will also work directly, so the code below is reusable.

And furthermore, the ending code can be replaced by:
```
draw_graph.add_driver_callback(p_callback, p_userdata, trackers,  usages);
```

As `VectorView` can automatically be constructed by `LocalVector` easily.

